{"id": "01M1VJF46TJCE8XPH5FY9W6EBS", "trailId": "01M0DNQ8XCZ8B0FB39BG34XAGZ", "repositoryId": "01KWZ6252FA5XEMQJYDQ5ZX6RQ", "reviewId": "01M1VJF45J9G9VP79CXF7WVDSY", "codeVersionId": "01M1VHXQ4AK5T403HF6H7FMZVJ", "actorId": "agent:trail-review", "actorDisplayName": null, "body": "`runWorkspaceRefresh` (and similarly `runWorkspaceRemove`) still does an unlocked load-modify-write of `workspace.json`, unlike the newly-locked `addWorkspaceRepoLocked`. A concurrent `workspace refresh`/`remove` racing a `setup`/`workspace add` on the same workspace can load a stale manifest and overwrite it, silently dropping the repo the locked call just added — the exact race class `addWorkspaceRepoLocked` was introduced to fix, just not closed for every writer of the file.", "severity": "medium", "confidence": 0.65, "status": "open", "statusReason": null, "statusActorId": null, "statusActorDisplayName": null, "statusChangedAt": null, "statusSource": null, "statusActorKind": null, "staleOutcome": "stale", "staleCheckedAt": "2026-09-06T16:02:16.444Z", "staleCheckedCodeVersionId": "01M1VQ9H62K4446TWXSA9WKR5Y", "clientId": "0ea00284528551b7defc327374eb8ed2", "clientIdHash": "a139b2eb5358ac4b1b2727af8e6cacb2dacd146f8ed0824f15fa6da1d04209d4", "createdAt": "2026-09-06T14:37:56.826Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T14:37:56.826Z", "location": {"id": "01M1VJF46TE1XMDXS4DMRPMCRE", "reviewCommentId": "01M1VJF46TJCE8XPH5FY9W6EBS", "codeVersionId": "01M1VHXQ4AK5T403HF6H7FMZVJ", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "internal/cli/workspace.go", "startLine": 750, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "	if err := writeWorkspaceManifest(opts.Env, manifest); err != nil {", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}}
{"id": "01M1VJF46NF19P6EDZGSE2HG9M", "trailId": "01M0DNQ8XCZ8B0FB39BG34XAGZ", "repositoryId": "01KWZ6252FA5XEMQJYDQ5ZX6RQ", "reviewId": "01M1VJF45J9G9VP79CXF7WVDSY", "codeVersionId": "01M1VHXQ4AK5T403HF6H7FMZVJ", "actorId": "agent:trail-review", "actorDisplayName": null, "body": "`applySetupRecordDefaults` seeds `setupOpts.daemonName` only from this repo's own (possibly nonexistent) per-repo record, never from the machine-wide watch plan. So on a machine where a different repo previously installed the daemon under a custom `--daemon-name`, a brand-new repo's plain, flag-less `entire-brain setup` resolves the default name, sees `installedDaemonName` report the custom name as installed, and `retireRenamedDaemon` uninstalls the shared, deliberately-named watcher, replacing it with the default — an uncommanded rename triggered by an unrelated repo's ordinary setup.", "severity": "medium", "confidence": 0.7, "status": "open", "statusReason": null, "statusActorId": null, "statusActorDisplayName": null, "statusChangedAt": null, "statusSource": null, "statusActorKind": null, "staleOutcome": "stale", "staleCheckedAt": "2026-09-06T16:02:16.444Z", "staleCheckedCodeVersionId": "01M1VQ9H62K4446TWXSA9WKR5Y", "clientId": "66540e23978d840bdc3e30a88667f0e6", "clientIdHash": "9dc8127bd5d6fe87ca8217914a79b9cb0b2a9fe673eb563f242627fbfe23d3a9", "createdAt": "2026-09-06T14:37:56.820Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T14:37:56.820Z", "location": {"id": "01M1VJF46NKYJA5PY12ZM74QAK", "reviewCommentId": "01M1VJF46NF19P6EDZGSE2HG9M", "codeVersionId": "01M1VHXQ4AK5T403HF6H7FMZVJ", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "internal/cli/setup.go", "startLine": 1326, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "func retireRenamedDaemon(ctx context.Context, setupOpts setupCommandOptions, old string, known bool, steps setupSteps, planErr error) string {", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}}
