{"id": "01M1WARNFA7J6M30JCRGHH9HH9", "trailId": "01M0DNQ8XCZ8B0FB39BG34XAGZ", "repositoryId": "01KWZ6252FA5XEMQJYDQ5ZX6RQ", "reviewId": "01M1WARNDF5X2K9EWNGACPW6DK", "codeVersionId": "01M1WAB0XEY0T4FWBG0P858WSY", "actorId": "agent:trail-review", "actorDisplayName": null, "body": "`runWorkspaceRefresh` now holds `acquireWorkspaceManifestLock` (10s timeout via `brainWriteLockTimeout`) across the entire `--full` refresh — multi-repo agent/semantic refresh, pattern corpus build, and graph snapshot — instead of just around the manifest read/write. Any concurrent `workspace add` or `setup` registration on the same workspace, which acquires the same lock with the same 10s timeout, will now spuriously fail with a lock-timeout error whenever a long-running refresh is in progress.", "severity": "medium", "confidence": 0.6, "status": "open", "statusReason": null, "statusActorId": null, "statusActorDisplayName": null, "statusChangedAt": null, "statusSource": null, "statusActorKind": null, "staleOutcome": "stale", "staleCheckedAt": "2026-09-06T22:15:02.974Z", "staleCheckedCodeVersionId": "01M1WCM3GNFC755CC0ZWGYBQ3E", "clientId": "c0b9c7983d9830834c5b8a010b51ec90", "clientIdHash": "0c5de7c3650028361e5688f12f0a9021d473c43ab5ccd7fa440e6bdad1ccae43", "createdAt": "2026-09-06T21:42:35.242Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T21:42:35.242Z", "location": {"id": "01M1WARNFAXEH5306C7XGQK5QF", "reviewCommentId": "01M1WARNFA7J6M30JCRGHH9HH9", "codeVersionId": "01M1WAB0XEY0T4FWBG0P858WSY", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "internal/cli/workspace.go", "startLine": 733, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "	lock, err := acquireWorkspaceManifestLock(opts.Env, workspaceName)", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}}
