{"id": "01M1VKBDXZKGC1T7QR0FRYBP9T", "trailId": "01M0DNQ8XCZ8B0FB39BG34XAGZ", "repositoryId": "01KWZ6252FA5XEMQJYDQ5ZX6RQ", "reviewId": "01M1VKBDXE2Q8YDK18RJNCPX6S", "codeVersionId": "01M1VJT00HQ4VTQYHEZA92Y1TP", "actorId": "agent:trail-review", "actorDisplayName": null, "body": "`trap cleanup EXIT INT TERM` combined with `cleanup`'s own `exit $status` causes double-firing: on SIGINT/SIGTERM, `cleanup` runs, calls `exit $status`, which re-triggers the EXIT trap and runs `cleanup` again, overwriting `status=$?` with the (typically 0) result of the `rm -rf`/fallback. Verified empirically — an interrupted run reports exit code 0 instead of 130/143, masking that the script was killed.", "severity": "medium", "confidence": 0.85, "status": "open", "statusReason": null, "statusActorId": null, "statusActorDisplayName": null, "statusChangedAt": null, "statusSource": null, "statusActorKind": null, "staleOutcome": "stale", "staleCheckedAt": "2026-09-06T19:58:46.046Z", "staleCheckedCodeVersionId": "01M1W4TJ77TJQ6G1VQBGDNH437", "clientId": "f79acdf2be0dce6d2f0b97d1be39e0d8", "clientIdHash": "b6b021eb392856be484c51fac915049080ffe88c001165879f32ed3c6ab5f119", "createdAt": "2026-09-06T14:53:24.286Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T14:53:24.286Z", "location": {"id": "01M1VKBDXZHGX364Y1PK939DHV", "reviewCommentId": "01M1VKBDXZKGC1T7QR0FRYBP9T", "codeVersionId": "01M1VJT00HQ4VTQYHEZA92Y1TP", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "scripts/demo-agent-session.sh", "startLine": 142, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "trap cleanup EXIT INT TERM", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}}
{"id": "01M1VJF478QHW2V2JQF3S9W20M", "trailId": "01M0DNQ8XCZ8B0FB39BG34XAGZ", "repositoryId": "01KWZ6252FA5XEMQJYDQ5ZX6RQ", "reviewId": "01M1VJF45J9G9VP79CXF7WVDSY", "codeVersionId": "01M1VHXQ4AK5T403HF6H7FMZVJ", "actorId": "agent:trail-review", "actorDisplayName": null, "body": "After detecting a stray `entire-brain` process that survived the 30s grace period (`stray=$(pgrep ...)`), the script only logs it and sets `leaked=1`; it never kills the process. The subsequent `die` call fires the `EXIT` trap, which unconditionally `rm -rf`s `$trial_dir` while the detected orphan may still be alive and operating on files under that now-deleted directory.", "severity": "low", "confidence": 0.55, "status": "open", "statusReason": null, "statusActorId": null, "statusActorDisplayName": null, "statusChangedAt": null, "statusSource": null, "statusActorKind": null, "staleOutcome": "stale", "staleCheckedAt": "2026-09-06T16:02:16.444Z", "staleCheckedCodeVersionId": "01M1VQ9H62K4446TWXSA9WKR5Y", "clientId": "783e4384c55555f199c6b20b98867e60", "clientIdHash": "cb295491c7c1805f555e1eeb95e22cce1fab8e90e59a0f0ef8d76267b455e326", "createdAt": "2026-09-06T14:37:56.839Z", "updatedAt": "2026-09-06T14:37:56.839Z", "location": {"id": "01M1VJF478VGMJVQCPKZWYGAEY", "reviewCommentId": "01M1VJF478QHW2V2JQF3S9W20M", "codeVersionId": "01M1VHXQ4AK5T403HF6H7FMZVJ", "granularity": "line", "filePath": "scripts/trial-setup.sh", "startLine": 300, "startColumn": null, "endLine": null, "endColumn": null, "selectedText": "	waited=$((waited + 1))", "nearbyText": null, "language": null}}
